cuems-power-bridge (0.3.0-4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * displays: add projector brightness presets over Epson ESC/VP21
    (ESC/VP.net, TCP 3629) -- a second control channel beside PJLink power,
    which has no brightness command. New `POST /brightness?level=<name>`
    (query string or JSON body) fans a configured ESC/VP21 command across an
    opt-in fleet; 200 all-applied / 207 partial / 502 all-failed /
    400 unknown_level / 503 no_brightness_devices. Generic + config-driven:
    `brightness.<level>.command` maps a level name to an ESC/VP21 verb, and
    `projector.N.brightness` (+ optional `escvp_password` / `escvp_port`) opts
    a device in -- no install-specific values in code, a no-op where
    unconfigured. Adds `displays/escvp.py` (HELLO + plaintext-password auth,
    trailing-header drain, CR/LF command sanitisation, dry_run, bounded
    timeout), `DeviceDef` brightness fields, a SEPARATE `_brightness_drivers`
    fleet in DisplayManager with per-device error isolation + startup
    validation, and three `/status` keys (`brightness_levels`,
    `brightness_devices`, `last_brightness_level`). Tests:
    tests/test_escvp.py (12) + tests/test_brightness.py (17).

