cuems-power-bridge (0.3.0-3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * displays: decouple projector power-on from project load. New
    `projector_power_on_on_start` global powers displays ON at bridge startup
    (independent of `projector_power_on_on_load`) so they warm up in parallel
    with node-wait / auto-load, plus an on-demand `POST /poweron`. Startup and
    on-load paths share the fire-and-forget task and dedup against each other.
  * autoload: new `auto_play` global (default false). After a successful
    auto-load (project loaded AND armed), optionally send
    `/engine/command/go` automatically so an unattended/kiosk controller
    plays from a cold boot. Fires only after the bridge's own auto-load
    (never a manual/editor load), waits bounded for armed, skips if the
    project is already running, and is cancelled on stop() and the shutdown
    path so a pending GO can't fire mid-power-off. Unit tests added
    (tests/test_bridge_autoplay.py).

